          "text": "Spend this period concentrated most heavily in $finding:top_spending_category.period, which totaled $finding:top_spending_category.value across $finding:top_spending_category.n transactions, while $finding:lowest_spending_category.period brought up the rear at just $finding:lowest_spending_category.value. The single largest charge was $finding:largest_single_transaction.value, posted on $finding:largest_single_transaction.period."
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_d",
          "op": "SECTION",
          "refs": [],
          "text": "Category breakdown"
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_e",
          "op": "EXPLAIN",
          "refs": ["top_spending_category", "lowest_spending_category", "segment_heterogeneity"],
          "text": "$finding:top_spending_category.period led every other category, its $finding:top_spending_category.value dwarfing the $finding:lowest_spending_category.value posted by $finding:lowest_spending_category.period. A $finding:segment_heterogeneity.test test puts a p-value of $finding:segment_heterogeneity.p_value on whether these category totals differ by more than chance, spanning group sizes of $finding:segment_heterogeneity.group_ns.",
          "anchor": "chart_category_spend"
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_f",
          "op": "CAVEAT",
          "refs": ["amount_sign_convention"],
          "anchor": "chart_category_spend"
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_g",
          "op": "EXPLAIN",
          "refs": ["daily_spend_trend", "daily_spend_step_change", "month_half_spend_comparison"],
          "text": "Daily spend moved $finding:daily_spend_trend.direction across the period, with an estimated slope of $finding:daily_spend_trend.slope_per_period per day and a p-value of $finding:daily_spend_trend.p_value on that trend. The sharpest jump between consecutive days measured $finding:daily_spend_step_change.baseline_spread, and splitting the month at its midpoint puts the late-period median at $finding:month_half_spend_comparison.late_median against an early-period median of $finding:month_half_spend_comparison.early_median, a $finding:month_half_spend_comparison.multiplier-fold difference.",
          "anchor": "chart_daily_spend"
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_h",
          "op": "EXPLAIN",
          "refs": ["weekday_weekend_spend_share"],
          "text": "Weekdays and weekends split the month's spend at $finding:weekday_weekend_spend_share.shares_pct, leaving $finding:weekday_weekend_spend_share.residual_pct unassigned to either bucket.",
          "anchor": "chart_day_of_week_spend"
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_i",
          "op": "INSIGHT",
          "refs": ["top_payee_by_spend", "largest_single_transaction", "spend_distribution"],
          "text": "Across individual transactions, $finding:top_payee_by_spend.period drew the most spend at $finding:top_payee_by_spend.value, a figure sitting against a distribution whose mean of $finding:spend_distribution.mean diverges from its median of $finding:spend_distribution.median by a skew of $finding:spend_distribution.skew. The largest single transaction, $finding:largest_single_transaction.value, sits well beyond that distribution's upper quartile of $finding:spend_distribution.p75."
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_j",
          "op": "CALLOUT",
          "refs": ["largest_single_transaction", "spend_distribution"],
          "text": "That $finding:largest_single_transaction.value charge on $finding:largest_single_transaction.period is the month's clearest outlier, standing apart from a spend distribution whose interquartile range runs from $finding:spend_distribution.p25 to $finding:spend_distribution.p75."
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_k",
          "op": "METHOD",
          "refs": ["daily_spend_trend", "segment_heterogeneity", "month_half_spend_comparison"],
          "text": "Category and payee totals were attestation-weighted before ranking; the daily trend uses an OLS fit across the period, the category comparison a $finding:segment_heterogeneity.test test, and the month split compares medians on either side of the period's midpoint."
        },
        {
          "id": "pn_msqv3drb_l",
          "op": "CONCLUSION",
          "refs": ["top_spending_category", "daily_spend_trend", "weekday_weekend_spend_share"],
          "text": "$finding:top_spending_category.period remains the month's dominant spend category at $finding:top_spending_category.value, set against a daily spend trend that moved $finding:daily_spend_trend.direction and a weekday/weekend split of $finding:weekday_weekend_spend_share.shares_pct."
        }
